---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Change text, corner, size, color, order or tags of objects. The objects are the linked object and every --object.
Moving a frame moves its content. It prints one line per changed object with @N and its link.

USAGE
  holst object edit <board> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board: id, link or part of its name

FLAGS
      --object object        An object, repeat for several: id, link, @N or the first 8 characters of its id
  -w, --workspace ws         Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --text text            The new text; lines become paragraphs; unchanged by default
      --text-format format   How the new text is read: plain, or markdown for headings, lists, checkboxes, links and bold, italic, strike marks; plain by default
      --at x,y               The new top-left corner in board units; unchanged by default
      --size wxh             The new size as width x height, e.g. 260x160; unchanged by default
  -c, --color color          The new fill, or an arrow's line color: a palette token, e.g. yellow4; unchanged by default
      --shape shape          Change a shape's kind, e.g. ellipse, flowchart-decision or bpmn-gateway; unchanged by default
      --stroke color         A shape's outline color: a palette token, e.g. gray12; unchanged by default
      --stroke-width n       A shape's outline width, 0 to 10; unchanged by default
      --stroke-style style   A shape's outline: solid, dashed or dotted; unchanged by default
      --radius n             A shape's corner radius, at most as the shape's size allows; unchanged by default
      --opacity n            A shape's fill opacity, 0.1 to 1; unchanged by default
      --order order          Where it stands among the objects: front or back; unchanged by default
      --tag tag              The object's tags, repeat for several; a new tag is made, '' clears; unchanged by default
      --items file           Many in one write: a JSON array or JSON lines file, - for stdin; its keys are the flags of one call
  -n, --dry-run              Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst o edit "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4 --text "Ask design by Friday"
  $ holst o edit "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4 --object e5f6a7b8 -c yellow4 --order front
  $ holst o edit "Roadmap" --items fixes.json

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
